11. Placement interview questions
Q1. What is clustering?
Clustering is an unsupervised learning technique that groups similar data points based on their features.
Q2. What is the difference between K-Means and DBSCAN?
K-Means groups points around centroids and requires the number of clusters to be specified. DBSCAN groups dense regions and can identify noise points without requiring the number of clusters in advance.
Q3. What is a centroid in K-Means?
A centroid is the mean position of the data points assigned to a cluster.
Q4. What is PCA?
PCA is a linear dimensionality reduction technique that transforms features into principal components ordered by explained variance.
Q5. What is the elbow method?
The elbow method compares clustering costs for different values of K and looks for a point where increasing K yields diminishing improvements.
Q6. What is the difference between clustering and classification?
Clustering discovers groups without supplied target labels, whereas classification learns to predict predefined classes using labeled examples.
